{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset"],"declarations":63,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.threading_cost_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.threading_cost_unique","kind":"theorem","line":802,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L802-L822","doc":"Threading cost uniqueness: two reductions of the same augmented braid\nyield identical normal forms — again **conditionally** on `hgs`, for the\nsame reason as `heckeCost_well_defined`, and again vacuous for this system.\nThe unconditional form is\n`HeckeCompletion.heckeCompleted_threading_cost_unique`. The \"no quasi-zeros\"\nhypothesis is discharged here: `HeckeGen (n+1)` has a generator, so the free\nalgebra on it has none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":778,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L778-L800","doc":"Normal forms of a Hecke algebra element are unique — **conditionally on\nthe system being a GS basis**, which is now an explicit hypothesis rather\nthan the deleted axiom. `NotAGSBasis.hecke_not_gs_basis_four` shows the\nhypothesis is unsatisfiable at `n = 4` for `heckeRewritingSystem` as it\nstands, so this statement is vacuous as it applies to *this* system.\n\nThe Bokut–Shiao completion has since been added and proved:\n`HeckeCompletion.heckeCompleted_normalForm_unique` is this statement against\n`heckeCompletedRewritingSystem`, with the hypothesis discharged. Use that\none; this stays because it is stated at the level the abstract framework\nworks at, and because deleting it would erase the record of why the\nuncompleted system cannot support it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":770,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L770-L774","doc":"The Hecke cost is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost","kind":"def","line":761,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L761-L768","doc":"The Hecke cost of an element: the sum of absolute values of\ncoefficients across the entire support.\n\n`heckeCost(f) = Σ_{m ∈ supp(f)} |f.coeff(m)|`\n\nThis is well-defined because `support` is a `Finset`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.augmentedBraidElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.augmentedBraidElement","kind":"def","line":745,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L745-L757","doc":"The augmented braid element for threading: prepend the photon\nstrand above the hadron, then un-braid below.\n\n`augmentedBraid β_H = σ_n · σ_{n-1} · … · σ₁ · β_H · σ₁⁻¹ · … · σ_n⁻¹`\n\nIn the `B_{n+1}` embedding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braidToAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braidToAlg","kind":"def","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L715-L743","doc":"Embed a braid word (list of signed generators) into `AlgElement`\nby left-multiplying each generator's embedding successively.\n\nUses `AlgElement.leftMulGen` from AlgOps.lean to avoid needing\ngeneral convolution.  For a word `[g₁, g₂, g₃]`:\n`braidToAlg = embed(g₁) · embed(g₂) · embed(g₃)`\n\nSince each embedded generator is itself an `AlgElement` (not a single\ngenerator), we need `AlgElement` multiplication.  We approximate this\nby folding over the word, using `leftMulWord` for the singleton terms\nand `add`/`smul` for the inverse terms.\n\nFor positive generators (which are singletons `[σᵢ]`), the\nmultiplication is simply `leftMulGen σᵢ`.  For negative generators\n(which are 2-term sums), we distribute the multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedGenerator","kind":"def","line":702,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L702-L713","doc":"Embed a signed braid generator into `AlgElement`.\nPositive index → singleton monomial.\nNegative index → Hecke inverse.\n\nRequires `[NeZero n]` so that `_ % n < n` is well-defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedNegativeGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedNegativeGen","kind":"def","line":686,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L686-L700","doc":"Embed a negative generator `σᵢ⁻¹` via the Hecke relation inverse:\n`σᵢ⁻¹ = (q⁻¹ - q)σᵢ + q⁻¹`.\n\nDerived from `σᵢ² = (q-q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1`:\n`σᵢ · ((q⁻¹-q)σᵢ + q⁻¹) = (q⁻¹-q)σᵢ² + q⁻¹σᵢ`\n`= (q⁻¹-q)((q-q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1) + q⁻¹σᵢ`\n`= -(q-q⁻¹)²σᵢ + (q⁻¹-q) + q⁻¹σᵢ`\n`= (-(q²-2+q⁻²) + q⁻¹)σᵢ + (q⁻¹-q)`\nAfter simplification, this equals `1` (the identity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedPositiveGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedPositiveGen","kind":"def","line":681,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L681-L684","doc":"Embed a positive generator `σᵢ` as the singleton monomial `[σᵢ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_is_gs_basis_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_is_gs_basis_false","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L665-L677","doc":"**The former axiom `hecke_is_gs_basis` is false.**\n\nIt asserted `∀ n (hn : 0 < n) (hp : HeckeParams), IsGrobnerShirshovBasis …` for\n`heckeRewritingSystem`; `n = 4` refutes it. The axiom has been deleted from\nthis file: with the repaired definitions it would have made the library\ninconsistent, not merely optimistic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hecke_not_gs_basis_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hecke_not_gs_basis_four","kind":"theorem","line":650,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L650-L661","doc":"**The Hecke relations are not a Gröbner–Shirshov basis at `n = 4`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":641,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L641-L648","doc":"The S-polynomial is a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":631,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L631-L639","doc":"No rule of the system applies to `σ₃σ₂σ₁σ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":621,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L621-L629","doc":"No rule of the system applies to `σ₂σ₃σ₂σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":618,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L618-L619","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L615-L616","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":612,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L612-L613","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":609,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L609-L610","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L606-L607","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":603,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L603-L604","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_support","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L569-L596","doc":"Everything the S-polynomial is supported on is one of three words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_coeff_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_coeff_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L556-L567","doc":"The S-polynomial has coefficient `1` at `σ₂σ₃σ₂σ₁`: it is not zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lc","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L551-L554","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lc","kind":"theorem","line":546,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L546-L549","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₂","kind":"def","line":544,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L544-L544","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₁","kind":"def","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L542-L543","doc":"The two irreducible words the S-polynomial is supported on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_mem","kind":"theorem","line":536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L536-L540","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_mem","kind":"theorem","line":530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L530-L534","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.oc","kind":"def","line":519,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L519-L528","doc":"The overlap composition on the ambient word `σ₃σ₂σ₃σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lm","kind":"theorem","line":516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L516-L517","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lm","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L513-L514","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc","kind":"def","line":510,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L510-L511","doc":"The far-commutation rule for `(σ₃, σ₁)`; `lm = σ₃σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb","kind":"def","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L507-L508","doc":"The Yang–Baxter rule for the adjacent pair `(σ₂, σ₃)`; `lm = σ₃σ₂σ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hn4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hn4","kind":"theorem","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L504-L505","doc":"`0 < 4`, once, so that every statement below is about the same system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L468-L473","doc":"The unit is in normal form for the Hecke system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_does_not_reduce_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_does_not_reduce_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L458-L466","doc":"**The unit does not reduce to zero.**  This is the acceptance test for the\nthree repairs of `Basic.lean` (bean qou-auq3): under the old definitions\nevery element reduced to zero, so `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` was satisfied by\nevery rewriting system whatsoever. It is not any more. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gs_basis_of_empty_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gs_basis_of_empty_lm","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L330-L454","doc":"**A rule that is a non-zero scalar collapses the GS property.**\n\nIf some rule's leading monomial is `[]` and its constant term is invertible —\nwhich is exactly what the removed sentinel `⟨ofTerms [([], q)], _⟩` was — then\n*every* element of the free algebra reduces to zero and\n`IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` holds for any generators, any order, any rules. The\npredicate then distinguishes nothing.\n\nTwo remarks on the statement, relative to the version proved against the\n*unrepaired* definitions:\n\n* the hypothesis `lc ≠ 0` is new and is needed. Previously\n  `SingleStepReduction` imposed no algebraic condition, so a rule with empty\n  leading monomial rewrote anything to anything; now a step must subtract an\n  actual multiple of the relation, and a relation with vanishing constant term\n  subtracts nothing. The removed sentinel satisfies it (`q > 0`).\n* the support hypothesis one might expect — that the relation is supported on\n  `[]` alone — is *not* needed: `AdmissibleOrder.not_lt_nil` shows the empty\n  word is the minimum of every admissible order, so a relation whose leading\n  monomial is `[]` has no other monomials at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L320-L326","doc":"No rule of the Hecke system has an empty leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L306-L318","doc":"Every rule of `heckeRewritingSystem` is one of the three families, and its\nleading monomial is the explicit word listed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_heckeRewritingSystem_rules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_heckeRewritingSystem_rules","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L281-L304","doc":"**Every rule of `heckeRewritingSystem` is one of the three relations**, with\nits indices and its side condition. This is the inversion of the three `_mem`\nlemmas, and unlike `heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases` it lands on the rule itself,\nwhich is what any statement about `spoly` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L252-L262","doc":"`lm(σᵢσⱼ − σⱼσᵢ) = [σᵢ, σⱼ]` when `j < i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L239-L250","doc":"`lm(σᵢσⱼσᵢ − σⱼσᵢσⱼ) = [σⱼ, σᵢ, σⱼ]` when `i < j` — the *reverse* of the\norientation claimed by `yangBaxterRelation`'s docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L227-L237","doc":"`lm(σᵢ² − (q−q⁻¹)σᵢ − 1) = [σᵢ, σᵢ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_lex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_lex","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L221-L225","doc":"Equal-length words compare lexicographically by generator rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_length","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L217-L219","doc":"Shorter words are smaller in the deg-lex order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L157-L188","doc":"The complete Hecke rewriting system for `H_n(q)`.\nCollects all Hecke, Yang–Baxter, and far-commutativity relations\nfor generators `σ₀, …, σ_{n-1}`.\n\n**Requires `0 < n`, and carries no sentinel rule.** An earlier version\nappended `⟨ofTerms [([], q)], _⟩` to satisfy `RewritingSystem.nonempty` at\n`n = 0`. That rule's support is `{[]}`, so its leading monomial is the empty\nword, and `[] <:+: m` holds for every `m` — which made `isNormalForm` false\nfor every element with non-empty support and collapsed the whole GS property\n(`gs_basis_of_empty_lm` below proves the collapse). With `0 < n` the Hecke\nrelation for `σ₀` supplies the non-emptiness instead, and every leading\nmonomial is a genuine word. `n = 0` is no loss: `H_0(q)` has no generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L146-L155","doc":"The far-commutativity relation for non-adjacent generators:\n`σᵢσⱼ - σⱼσᵢ = 0` when `|i-j| ≥ 2`, oriented so that the\nhigher-index generator comes first (lm = `[σᵢ, σⱼ]` with `i > j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L135-L144","doc":"The Yang–Baxter relation for adjacent generators `σᵢ, σᵢ₊₁`:\n`σᵢσᵢ₊₁σᵢ - σᵢ₊₁σᵢσᵢ₊₁ = 0`, oriented as\n`σᵢσᵢ₊₁σᵢ → σᵢ₊₁σᵢσᵢ₊₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L119-L133","doc":"The Hecke relation for generator `σᵢ`:\n`σᵢ² - (q - q⁻¹)σᵢ - 1 = 0`, oriented as\n`σᵢ² → (q - q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1`.\n\nAs an `AlgElement`: leading monomial `[σᵢ, σᵢ]` with coefficient 1,\nplus `[σᵢ]` with coefficient `-(q - q⁻¹)`, plus `[]` with\ncoefficient `-1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L115-L115","doc":"`q ≠ 1` (non-classical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L113-L113","doc":"`q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.mk","kind":"ctor","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams","kind":"structure","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L108-L115","doc":"Deformation parameter for the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L99-L104","doc":"The deg-lex admissible order on Hecke monomials.\nConstructed via the generic `mkDegLexOrder` from AlgOps.lean,\nreusing the same proof infrastructure as `degLexOrder` for\n`SU2Gen` in NormalForms.lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank_injective","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L92-L97","doc":"The rank function for `HeckeGen n` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.σ","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L86-L88","doc":"Shorthand: create a Hecke generator from a natural number index.\nReturns the generator `σ_i` when `i < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L83-L84","doc":"The rank of a Hecke generator (for deg-lex ordering). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen.decEq","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen","kind":"instance","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.index","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Generator index (0-based). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen","kind":"structure","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L76-L81","doc":"Generator type for the Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`.\nFor `n` strands, there are `n` generators `σ₀,…,σ_{n-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}